<title>GERMANY: AMV H1 PREMIUMS RISE 1.2 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>AMV H1 PREMIUMS RISE 1.2 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>AACHEN, Germany 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group gross premium income	     1,200   up 1.2 pct</p>
<p>    Capital investments			3,100   up 13.3 pct</p>
<p>    Staff					  3,391   down 2.7 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurer is Aachener und Muenchener Versicherung AG, a unit of the AMB Holding group. The company also said in its interim report it was fully satisfied with its performance in the first half and that it expected a higher profit for the full year. AMV reported a net profit of 47.3 million marks in 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
